534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433155 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433159 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433162 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433163 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433165 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433170 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433170 1077 "selection" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433170 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433163 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433170 1079 #uuid "375de494-0474-59f2-a5cb-d4f2d3d924b6" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433171 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433160 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433171 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433161 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433171 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433166 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433171 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433167 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433171 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433169 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433171 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433171 1077 "selection" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433171 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433166 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433171 1079 #uuid "72992156-232d-5e59-a853-f830c746fc70" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433156 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433157 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433158 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433164 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433168 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433172 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433172 1077 "selection" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433172 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433164 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433172 1079 #uuid "bb45a89e-3bde-5251-b24c-b1bd686d3497" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433173 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433170 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433173 1069 "q-34711" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433173 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433173 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nII. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n\nIII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433173 1072 #uuid "46f6694f-8103-554b-a6d3-9a98e8c2973d" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433173 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement III is false, while statements I and II are true." 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433174 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433171 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433174 1069 "q-181534" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433174 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433174 1071 "Let $I=N$ and ${S}_{i}=(0,\\frac{2i}{2i-1}),$ then ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}=$" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433174 1072 #uuid "f0553cd0-23ab-5839-b32e-fb9520332a9c" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433174 1074 "The intersection of a family of indexed sets $\\{{A}_{i}\\}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${S}_{1}=(0,2)$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have ${S}_{2}=(0,\\frac{4}{3})$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${S}_{3}=(0,\\frac{6}{5})$\n\n- if $i=4,$ we have ${S}_{4}=(0,\\frac{8}{7})$\n\nand so on.\n\nNotice that as $i$ increases, \n\n- the left endpoint of the intervals is $0$ for all the sets,\n\n- the right endpoint of the intervals is greater than $1$ and approaches $1$ from the right, never reaching it.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}=(0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433175 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433172 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433175 1069 "q-126832" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433175 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433175 1071 "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨t+3,\\,1-t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ at the point $P(4,0,1),$ valid for all real values of $u?$" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433175 1072 #uuid "f8d1a00d-2251-5725-a02b-3b2319318fd8" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433175 1074 "The point $P(4,0,1)$ is at the tip of $r(t)$ for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point,  the vector ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nR(u)=r({t}_{0})+u\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨4,0,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨t+3,1-t,{t}^{2}⟩ & =⟨4,0,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the components yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}t+3=4 \\\\ 1-t=0 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the first equation, we get $t=1.$ This value also satisfies the other equation. Therefore,  $P(4,0,1)$ is at the tip of the vector $r(1).$\n\nWe calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨1,-1,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point  $P(4,0,1)$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨4,0,1⟩+u⟨1,-1,2⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433176 1062 #uuid "48656a2f-f00d-59d7-ab86-aed535a53970" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433176 1063 #edb/ref 17592186305140 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433177 1058 #edb/ref 17592186433178 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433177 1062 #uuid "4e0ba4b6-098e-52a4-8d07-3abaebd61f9d" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433177 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265816 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433178 1058 #edb/ref 17592186433179 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433178 1062 #uuid "bfd67c17-3475-580b-bd20-fca8a021b88f" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433178 1063 #edb/ref 17592186433173 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433179 1058 #edb/ref 17592186433180 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433179 1062 #uuid "e2bc513d-bf4c-58fb-89b6-b71a9d225e16" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433179 1063 #edb/ref 17592186433175 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433180 1058 #edb/ref 17592186433176 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433180 1062 #uuid "e944ef5c-0b09-5365-be49-0201874b1f7b" 13194139534697 17592186045417 true] [17592186433180 1063 #edb/ref 17592186433174 13194139534697 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-26d80ffd-784b-5cee-95c0-c712aba5c5de" 17592186433154 "answer-008275fa-715e-57ea-bc82-5a6102db2a5d" 17592186433155 "answer-01f9c607-a00d-5f26-9c10-092b5fb19c5d" 17592186433156 "answer-35a27e71-b8e5-549e-97ab-d093597bcb5b" 17592186433157 "answer-3e141537-57e7-5d24-b24a-a74eaabb1717" 17592186433158 "answer-59f9131e-98fe-5931-bf40-b384cfc12aca" 17592186433159 "answer-5f9404ea-93a6-52ed-a4d6-367243aa4e24" 17592186433160 "answer-62c57b84-928c-5133-b786-712eefb8d26e" 17592186433161 "answer-75750201-9871-5333-9d36-628baad463f0" 17592186433162 "answer-75b5793f-7a42-5e9f-b867-97cb0a94ee05" 17592186433163 "answer-7c3eb033-52d1-5